.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt ROUTE 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm route
.Nd list, add and delete IPv4 routes through the net: service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm show
.Nm
.Cm add Cm default Ar gateway Op Ar interface
.Nm
.Cm add Cm host Ar address Op Ar interface
.Nm
.Cm add Ar destination Ns Op / Ns Ar prefix Op Ar interface
.Nm
.Cm delete Cm default Op Ar interface
.Nm
.Cm delete Cm host Ar address Op Ar interface
.Nm
.Cm delete Ar destination Ns Op / Ns Ar prefix Op Ar interface
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and changes the live IPv4 route table through the
.Dq net:
control channel. With no command, or with
.Cm show ,
it lists every route with its destination, optional gateway, interface and flags.
.Pp
The
.Cm add
forms install a default route (prefix 0) through
.Ar gateway ,
a host route (prefix 32), or a network route with an explicit prefix. A destination without a
prefix is a host route. The address is masked to the prefix before the request is sent, so
.Dq 198.51.100.5/24
and
.Dq 198.51.100.0/24
name the same route. The
.Cm delete
forms remove the exact destination and prefix. When the interface is omitted,
.Dq lo
is used.
.Pp
The tool uses the
.Dv RouteList ,
.Dv RouteAddOn
and
.Dv RouteDelOn
control requests. A malformed IPv4 address, a prefix outside
.Dv 0..=32
or an invalid interface name is rejected before any request. An unknown interface, a failed
delete or a server-side rejection is reported and the tool exits non-zero.
.Pp
No raw socket is opened and no routing daemon is required.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr netstat 8 ,
.Xr ping 8 ,
.Xr netd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
